# Host tests (Option A)

Firmware logic that does not need Arduino runs on the host with Unity.

```bash
pio test -e native
```

That env compiles only `src/settings/validate.cpp`. It does not flash the ESP32.

`pio run` builds firmware only (`default_envs`). Native is **`pio test -e native`**, not `pio run -e native`.

JS package tests (unchanged by this suite):

```bash
npm test --prefix packages/tiny-engineer-cursor
```
